    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Explain why $\\{x\\in\\mathbb{Z}\\text{ where }8<x<2\\}=\\varnothing$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No integer can be both greater than $8$ and less than $2$, so the set has no elements.",
      "worked": "The conditions $x>8$ and $x<2$ must both hold. No real number, and therefore no integer, satisfies them simultaneously. Hence $\\{x\\in\\mathbb{Z}\\text{ where }8<x<2\\}=\\varnothing$.",
